  (text "The two bays.  Each has the Framework input-module contacts (J2 = bay 1, inner one; J3 = bay 2, outer one):\n1 GND, 2 VCC_5V (up to 500 mA), 3 USB D-, 4 BOARD_ID (pulled to ground in the module), 5 USB D+,\n6 SLEEP# (3.3 V = host awake), 7 GND, 8 VCC_3V3 (up to 100 mA)\nA bay is powered only while a module sits in it, as on the Framework Laptop 16 (whose input deck stays off until\nevery pogo connector is covered): BOARD_ID is pulled up by 2.2 M; with a module in place its resistor (68 k - 560 k)\nholds the pin below 0.7 V, the 2N7002 turns off and the bay's enable line charges through 1 M into 1 uF - both\nswitches come on about 0.6 s later.  So pins that are uncovered (an empty bay, a module sliding in or out over the\ncontacts) carry no power.  Pull the module: BOARD_ID rises, the FET discharges the enable line at once.\nCurrent limits: 5 V 0.62 A (11 k), 3.3 V 0.40 A (17 k; the switch's smallest limit)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d3140587-797a-54d5-9e03-d06ccb15f350"))
